From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RicemanRhys <176650384+RicemanRhys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:12:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local-only: xbox_d3d8 skips binds and uploads that change
 nothing (perf only, identical output)

- A record of what the draws last bound on the D3D11 context (shaders,
  input layout, constant buffers, blend/depth/rasterizer states, samplers,
  vertex/index buffers, topology); a bind of the object already bound is
  skipped. Code outside xbox_d3d8 that binds on the same context puts back
  what it found (twoc's present passes, Dear ImGui's backend), and the
  gamma pass's command list restores the context state.
- Samplers: found by a hash of their description instead of a scan of the
  cache for each of 4 stages at every draw; a stage whose description is
  its last draw's keeps its bound object.
- The fixed-function pixel shader and its constants are no longer built
  and bound at every draw only to be replaced by the combiners' shader;
  d3d8_shaders_prepare_draw takes the combiners' when they have one.
- The combiner and fixed-function pixel constants are built locally and
  uploaded only when they differ from what the buffer holds.
- UP draws: the rings stay bound at offset 0 (vertices placed at a
  multiple of the stride, drawn with a start/base vertex and start index);
  the stream source and indices are no longer bound again after each UP
  draw: DrawPrimitive/DrawIndexedPrimitive bind them themselves.
- The A8 smoke test sets each path's pixel shader token and binds through
  the record, as the library now does.

Under the twoc notes' 18.63 rule refinement (perf-only changes in
xbox_d3d8, local, never pushed); twoc notes 18.79.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
